nication again it's all  speculation at this point but but I do I  do understand the crew concept I think  you keep the crews together as much as  possible the XFL with the kickoff or  there's no onside kick and now the NFL  is toying with the fourth and 15 instead  of the onside kick what do you think of  this yeah it's a very positive positive  you know look I'm four I'm all for  change but I don't like change for just  change sake right I want I like the  tradition of the game I still think the  onside kick there's a chance you look at  the numbers yeah in 2000 in 2018 it had  dropped drastically because of the rules  changes but last year you know was up up  you know twelve thirteen percent which  is which is its historical number  I like the onside kick I don't like a  gimmick fourth and 15 I just feel like  there's a lot of you know unintended  consequences we have to see you know is  it a safer play nobody knows nobody  knows that fourth and 15 is safer than  an onside kick with the new rule  changes in terms of formation so I like  I like where it is I don't I understand  the reason I know we need teams to have  an opportunity to come back you want  closer games you want more exciting  finishes I just think there's a whole  host of things that have to be worked  out on 4th and 15 you know in that  situation what about penalties are you  replaying the down if the offense pushes  off and they get offensive past the  frame so we trying it again what about  the clock all of these different things  I think I would like for the league to  work those things out and and then and  then have a good healthy discussion over  the course of time before they implement  a drastic change like this Dean it's  always great to touch base with you tell  Mike that we said hello is prayer is he  behaving but you two live together right  I like that Dean thanks for joining us  that's Fox NFL rules analyst and he also  worked with the XFL

